# Comprehensive Project Audit & In-Depth Technical Review: Project LUMEN

## 1. Executive Summary & Verdict

**Project LUMEN** (*Lunar Multi-Sensor Registration Pipeline*) is an end-to-end photogrammetric and computer vision framework engineered to ingest, orthorectify, normalize, match, and register multi-sensor lunar imagery acquired by India's **Chandrayaan-2** orbiter:
* **OHRC** (*Orbiter High Resolution Camera*): ~0.12–0.29 m/pixel high-resolution panchromatic.
* **TMC-2** (*Terrain Mapping Camera-2*): ~5.0–5.48 m/pixel stereo panchromatic (fore/nadir/aft).
* **IIRS** (*Imaging Infrared Spectrometer*): ~25–80 m/pixel, 256-band hyperspectral cubes (712–5009 nm).

### Current Operational State: **Demo & Production Ready for Same-Sensor Stereo; Architecturally Ready for Cross-Sensor**
* **Test Suite**: **80 passed**, 2 skipped (GPU-only tests), **0 failures** across all modules.
* **Live Satellite Verification**: Successfully verified on real Chandrayaan-2 PDS4 data via [tests/test_pipeline.py:L218-L277](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/tests/test_pipeline.py#L218-L277), producing valid inlier correspondences on real lunar surface terrain.
* **The "No-Overlap" Data Constraint**: The pipeline's cross-sensor alignment logic is architecturally sound and mathematically complete; however, the sample data currently in [data/raw/](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/data/raw) targets geographically disjoint regions of the Moon (OHRC at Boguslawsky Crater, TMC-2 at the Lunar South Pole, IIRS at the Equator). The system strictly and correctly raises [NoOverlapError](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/lumen/preprocess/overlap_crop.py#L38-L44) rather than hallucinating false matches.

