## 2. Deep-Dive: 7-Stage Architectural Pipeline

The entire system is orchestrated by [RegistrationPipeline](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/lumen/pipeline/orchestrator.py#L129-L665). Each pair passes through 7 distinct stages:

```
[1. PDS4 Ingestion] ──────> [2. Orthorectification] ──────> [3. Geographic Overlap Crop]
(XML Metadata & Binary)     (GCP-to-EPSG:4326 Warping)       (Polygon/BBox Intersection)
                                                                       │
                                                                       ▼
[6. Outlier Rejection & Warp] <─── [5. Multi-Modal Matching] <─── [4. Photometric Normalization]
(MAGSAC++ & Phase Subpixel)        (Deep ORB/LightGlue vs RIFT2)   (Lommel-Seeliger & CLAHE)
         │
         ▼
[7. Sub-Pixel Evaluation & Export]
(RMSE, Inlier Ratio, SSIM, GeoTIFF)
```

### Stage 1: PDS4 Ingestion & Metadata Parsing
* **Files**: [pds4_parser.py](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/lumen/ingest/pds4_parser.py), [metadata.py](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/lumen/ingest/metadata.py).
* **Functionality**:
  * Ingests native ISRO PDS4 XML labels and companion binary raster payloads (`.img`, `.qub`).
  * Enforces strict schema extraction without silent defaults: `sun_azimuth`, `sun_elevation`, `solar_incidence`, `spacecraft_altitude`, `pixel_resolution`, and GCP sidecar paths (`_g_grd_d18.csv` or `_d_loc_d18_ard.img`).
  * Handles endianness and sensor-specific binary packing:
    * **OHRC**: 16-bit unsigned big-endian (`>u2`), reading calibrated radiance arrays.
    * **TMC-2**: 10-bit packed or 16-bit unpacked single-band rasters.
    * **IIRS**: 256-band Band-Sequential (`BSQ`) 32-bit float cubes (`<f4`).

### Stage 2: Orthorectification (GCP Geometric Reprojection)
* **File**: [orthorectify.py](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/lumen/preprocess/orthorectify.py).
* **Physics & Implementation**:
  * Planetary pushbroom images lack standard terrestrial camera RPCs; ISRO supplies regular Ground Control Point (GCP) grids: `(Longitude, Latitude, Pixel, Scan)`.
  * For IIRS, coordinates are embedded in a 2-band location image (`_d_loc_d18_ard.img`).
  * Constructs in-memory `rasterio` memory-file datasets with attached GCPs, projecting pixels into selenographic geographic coordinates (`EPSG:4326`) via Lanczos interpolation.
  * Handles polar longitude convergence via anisotropic angular spacing based on lunar radius ($R_{\text{moon}} = 1,737,400\text{ m}$).
  * **DEM Integration**: Samples elevation $z$ from LOLA/SELENE DEM datasets using bilinear interpolation, with partial-coverage warnings.

### Stage 3: Geographic Overlap Crop
* **File**: [overlap_crop.py](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/lumen/preprocess/overlap_crop.py).
* **Logic**:
  * Computes the 2D bounding-box intersection $[x_{\min}, y_{\min}, x_{\max}, y_{\max}]$ of both footprints in degrees.
  * If $\text{area}(\text{intersection}) / \text{area}(\text{footprint}) < 0.001$, raises `NoOverlapError`, identifying both sensor footprints.
  * Adds an optional safety margin buffer (default 5%) and extracts identical spatial extents, preventing out-of-bounds cross-matching.

### Stage 4: Radiometric & Photometric Normalization
* **Files**: [photometric.py](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/lumen/preprocess/photometric.py), [radiometric.py](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/lumen/preprocess/radiometric.py).
* **Physics Model**:
  * Lunar regolith exhibits strong coherent backscattering. Standard Lambertian reflectance models fail at oblique sun angles.
  * LUMEN applies the **Lommel-Seeliger scattering model**:
    $$\rho(\alpha, i, e) = \frac{\cos(i)}{\cos(i) + \cos(e)} f(\alpha)$$
  * Normalizes illumination across differing solar elevations ($5^\circ$ to $85^\circ$), followed by Contrast Limited Adaptive Histogram Equalization (**CLAHE**) with clip limit 2.0 and an $8 \times 8$ tile grid.

### Stage 5: Multi-Modal Feature Extraction & Matching
* **Files**: [deep_matcher.py](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/lumen/features/deep_matcher.py), [rift2.py](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/lumen/features/rift2.py), [iirs_pan.py](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/lumen/features/iirs_pan.py).
* **Dual Dispatch Engine**:
  * **Same-Sensor (TMC-to-TMC or OHRC-to-OHRC)**: Dispatches to **DeepMatcher** (SuperPoint + LightGlue), with automatic CPU fallback to OpenCV ORB + BFMatcher (Hamming distance + cross-check).
  * **Cross-Sensor (OHRC-to-TMC or TMC-to-IIRS)**: Dispatches to **RIFT2** (*Radiation-variation Insensitive Feature Transform 2*). Computes Log-Gabor phase congruency over 4 scales and 6 orientations, constructs Maximum Index Maps (MIM), and generates illumination-invariant descriptors.
  * **IIRS Hyperspectral Adaptation**: Raw 256-band IIRS cubes cannot be matched directly with visible imagery. [iirs_to_pan](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/lumen/features/iirs_pan.py) synthesizes an optical panchromatic proxy by computing a solar-irradiance-weighted average across bands 0–12 ($712–1000\text{ nm}$), which overlaps the red/NIR sensitivity of OHRC and TMC-2.

### Stage 6: Outlier Rejection & Sub-Pixel Transformation
* **Files**: [outlier_reject.py](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/lumen/geometry/outlier_reject.py), [subpixel.py](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/lumen/geometry/subpixel.py), [warp.py](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/lumen/registration/warp.py).
* **Transform Estimation**:
  * Evaluates putative keypoint correspondences using OpenCV `USAC_MAGSAC` (MAGSAC++) with 5,000 max iterations and 0.999 confidence to filter out false correspondences.
  * Passes inlier coordinates into a **Phase Cross-Correlation subpixel refiner** ([skimage.registration.phase_cross_correlation](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/lumen/geometry/subpixel.py#L10-L43)), achieving an upsampling factor of 100 on local $64 \times 64$ image patches.
  * Re-fits the final 2D projective homography matrix $H$ on refined points.
  * Warps the source image onto the reference image plane via perspective warping and writes out a spatial GeoTIFF carrying the exact reference CRS and affine transform.

### Stage 7: Sub-Pixel Quantitative Evaluation
* **File**: [metrics.py](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/lumen/evaluation/metrics.py).
* **Validation & Metrics**:
  * Calculates Root Mean Square Error ($\text{RMSE} = \sqrt{\text{RMSE}_x^2 + \text{RMSE}_y^2}$), Inlier Ratio ($\% = N_{\text{inliers}} / N_{\text{total}}$), Mean Absolute Error (MAE), and Structural Similarity Index (**SSIM**).
  * Generates visual diagnostic products: alternating checkerboard overlays and false-color RGB composites (Source in Red, Reference in Green).

