## 6. Recommendations & Technical Observations

1. **Cross-Sensor Real Data Provisioning**:
   * To demonstrate cross-sensor registration (e.g., OHRC-to-TMC or TMC-to-IIRS) on real data, acquire overlapping PDS4 products from ISRO's PRADAN portal covering the exact same lunar coordinate box (such as Boguslawsky Crater or Apollo landing sites).
2. **Terrain Relief & Thin-Plate Spline (TPS)**:
   * The project currently uses global projective homography ($3 \times 3$ matrix via MAGSAC++). As documented in [outlier_reject.py](file:///c:/Users/morbi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/isro-chandrayaan/lumen/geometry/outlier_reject.py#L28-L42), for footprints $>10\text{ km}$ or elevation relief $>500\text{ m}$, adding non-rigid Thin-Plate Spline interpolation (`scipy.interpolate.RBFInterpolator`) will account for local parallax displacements.
3. **GPU Acceleration**:
   * The test suite skipped the two GPU tests (`test_deep_matcher_detect_shape` and `test_deep_matcher_match_shape`) because CUDA was not active. When deployed on a machine with an NVIDIA GPU and PyTorch CUDA, SuperPoint + LightGlue will execute in $<200\text{ ms}$ per tile instead of running ORB on CPU.

